nThe columns in this sheet (and why each is needed):\n  • Value — the final number plotted on the website, in TWh.\n  • Gross inland — raw input from Eurostat (nrg_bal_c). This is the published series the indicator reports; no further breakdown is available in the source.\n  • ktoe → TWh — unit-conversion factor (ktoe → TWh). Needed because the source reports ktoe but the indicator is shown in TWh; multiplying by it only changes the unit, not the underlying quantity.\n\nFormula:\n  Value = Gross inland × ktoe → TWh\n\nEverything recomputes live — change a raw input and the plotted value (and any intermediate columns) update automatically, using the same formulas as the original source workbook.\n\nPost-report years — where the later numbers come from\n\nThe 2024 report''s underlying data stops at 2021. The rows for 2022, 2023 were added afterwards and are computed from their own inputs, which sit in the columns to the right; the Value formula switches to them by year, so the report years keep the report''s own derivation.\n\n  Source: Eurostat (nrg_bal_c) — the published figure for these years.\n  The raw input (\"Gross inland (ktoe)\") is that published figure expressed in the\n  source''s own unit, obtained through this sheet''s own conversion constants. It is\n  exact, not an estimate: the formula is linear in that input, so the constants\n  invert it uniquely, and recomputing the row returns the published figure.\n  These rows therefore use the same columns and the same formula as the report years.\n\n  Vintage: fetched/checked 2026-07-27."}'::jsonb),
  ('esabcc-e1-energy-supply-ghg', '{"columns":[{"header":"Value","source":"EEA / EU GHG inventory (UNFCCC CRF), EU-27","formula":{"expr":"IF(A >= 2023, ROUND(([env_air_gge CRF1A1] + [env_air_gge CRF1B]), 1), ([Power and heat]+[Petroleum refineries]+[Other (mining, gas transport, …)]+[Fugitive emissions]+[Total (reported, no breakdown)]))"}},{"header":"Power and heat","source":"CRF table (2023 submission): 1.A.1.a (total)"},{"header":"Petroleum refineries","source":"CRF table (2023 submission): 1.A.1.b (total)"},{"header":"Other (mining, gas transport, …)","source":"CRF table (2023 submission): 1.A.1.c (total)"},{"header":"Fugitive emissions","source":"EEA inventory CSV: 1.B (given as CO2e total)"},{"header":"Total (reported, no breakdown)","source":"EEA / EU GHG inventory (UNFCCC CRF), EU-27"},{"header":"env_air_gge CRF1A1","source":"Eurostat env_air_gge · geo=EU27_2020, unit=MIO_T, freq=A, airpol=GHG, src_crf=CRF1A1 · https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/statistics/1.0/data/env_air_gge?format=JSON&lang=EN&geo=EU27_2020&unit=MIO_T&freq=A&airpol=GHG&src_crf=CRF1A1"},{"header":"env_air_gge CRF1B","source":"Eurostat env_air_gge · geo=EU27_2020, unit=MIO_T, freq=A, airpol=GHG, src_crf=CRF1B · https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/statistics/1.0/data/env_air_gge?format=JSON&lang=EN&geo=EU27_2020&unit=MIO_T&freq=A&airpol=GHG&src_crf=CRF1B"}],"rows":[{"year":2005,"cells":[1489.230863547243,1196.7582458460263,123.98705961012415,63.04660429109262,105.43895380000001,0,null,null]},{"year":2006,"cells":[1494.1525158825912,1202.2871586886665,124.13657103932623,64.87433775459844,102.8544484,0,null,null]},{"year":2007,"cells":[1503.668459698837,1217.0337780451016,126.0325001798641,62.44737177387138,98.1548097,0,null,null]},{"year":2008,"cells":[1433.2435942120883,1154.0902877042429,123.85014069512097,58.663509052724464,96.63965676,0,null,null]},{"year":2009,"cells":[1325.2180586250024,1071.7236287739076,116.49915436559944,47.5994345354952,89.39584095,0,null,null]},{"year":2010,"cells":[1343.140081949834,1083.1597856188062,115.76435969146951,55.27381875955815,88.94211788000001,0,null,null]},{"year":2011,"cells":[1333.855474351209,1078.116924470295,113.0561118340927,54.42572005682139,88.25671799,0,null,null]},{"year":2012,"cells":[1315.8795544891916,1073.8854674238546,109.90615796098554,44.70565820435123,87.38227090000001,0,null,null]},{"year":2013,"cells":[1254.011429036105,1017.828197834809,107.89153983016224,42.0468901911337,86.24480118,0,null,null]},{"year":2014,"cells":[1189.7277066873407,959.9153430101976,104.83732149796218,41.65928805918095,83.31575412,0,null,null]},{"year":2015,"cells":[1196.674215239784,968.478226654539,105.92321766926835,39.550595105976775,82.72217581,0,null,null]},{"year":2016,"cells":[1168.5148838034108,943.7780432166106,105.36763183034792,39.970913676452234,79.39829508,0,null,null]},{"year":2017,"cells":[1162.1379242846829,941.4613738822286,103.0793338102074,38.79935441224699,78.79786218,0,null,null]},{"year":2018,"cells":[1098.782173842464,882.6337398417216,99.76282735267915,41.25780184806324,75.12780479999999,0,null,null]},{"year":2019,"cells":[973.8049218778422,765.3394265641642,100.06290830640184,39.931718417276095,68.47086859,0,null,null]},{"year":2020,"cells":[841.5181786759792,652.2738549169003,93.1745498914046,32.67368369767437,63.39609017,0,null,null]},{"year":2021,"cells":[901.6247143916128,716.9830013629618,92.82853754286684,30.63507096578415,61.17810452,0,null,null]},{"year":2022,"cells":[924.3341574,0,0,0,0,924.3341574,null,null]},{"year":2023,"cells":[746.3,null,null,null,null,null,698.41559,47.89066]},{"year":2024,"cells":[689.1,null,null,null,null,null,642.41481,46.71211]}],"derivation":"Energy supply GHG emissions  (Mt CO₂eq)\n\nWhat it measures: ESABCC progress indicator E1. Total energy supply emissions: public power & heat, refineries and other energy industries. Fit-for-55 MIX gives the 2030 benchmark.\n\nHow it''s calculated:\n  1. Add up Power and heat, Petroleum refineries, Other, Fugitive emissions, and Total.\n\nWhy it''s done this way:\n  This is an accounting identity: the source reports these categories as mutually exclusive and exhaustive, so their sum is the total by construction — no modelling assumption is introduced, only disaggregated official data are re-aggregated.\n\n⚠ Caveat:\n  The sectoral breakdown is available 2005–2021; the 2022 point uses the reported total only (the four components are blank that year).\n\nThe columns in this sheet (and why each is needed):\n  • Value — the final number plotted on the website, in Mt CO₂eq.\n  • Power and heat — raw input from CRF table (2023 submission): 1.A.1.a (total). It is one of the source categories that are added together to form the total, so it has to be captured to reproduce the figure.\n  • Petroleum refineries — raw input from CRF table (2023 submission): 1.A.1.b (total). It is one of the source categories that are added together to form the total, so it has to be captured to reproduce the figure.\n  • Other — raw input from CRF table (2023 submission): 1.A.1.c (total). It is one of the source categories that are added together to form the total, so it has to be captured to reproduce the figure.\n  • Fugitive emissions — raw input from EEA inventory CSV: 1.B (given as CO2e total). It is one of the source categories that are added together to form the total, so it has to be captured to reproduce the figure.\n  • Total — raw input from EEA / EU GHG inventory (UNFCCC CRF), EU-27. It is one of the source categories that are added together to form the total, so it has to be captured to reproduce the figure.\n\nFormula:\n  Value = (Power and heat + Petroleum refineries + Other + Fugitive emissions + Total)\n\nEverything recomputes live — change a raw input and the plotted value (and any intermediate columns) update automatically, using the same formulas as the original source workbook.\n\nPost-report years — where the later numbers come from\n\nThe 2024 report''s underlying data stops at 2022. The rows for 2023, 2024 were added afterwards and are computed from their own inputs, which sit in the columns to the right; the Value formula switches to them by year, so the report years keep the report''s own derivation.\n\n  Source: Eurostat env_air_gge · CRF 1.A.1 + 1.B (energy supply) · EU27_2020\n  Note:   Public power/heat + fugitive emissions; CO₂-eq (Mt).\n  Every input column carries its exact dataset query in its source field.\n\n  Vintage: fetched/checked 2026-07-27."}'::jsonb),
  ('esabcc-e2-fossil-power-share', '{"columns":[{"header":"Value","source":"Eurostat energy balances (EU-27 gross electricity generation)","formula":{"expr":"IF(A >= 2023, ROUND([Report baseline 2022 (%)] * ([Numerator · nrg_bal_peh C0000X0350-0370] + [Numerator · nrg_bal_peh P1000] + [Numerator · nrg_bal_peh S2000] + [Numerator · nrg_bal_peh O4000XBIO] + [Numerator · nrg_bal_peh G3000]) / ([Denominator · nrg_bal_peh TOTAL]) / [Live source at 2022 (same basis as the columns left)], 2), (([Solid fossil fuels]+[Natural & manufactured gases]+[Oil products & other fossils]) / [Total]) * [fraction → % (× 100)])"}},{"header":"Solid fossil fuels","source":"See 4bis tab for sources and categorisation details"},{"header":"Natural & manufactured gases","source":"See 4bis tab for sources and categorisation details"},{"header":"Oil products & other fossils","source":"See 4bis tab for sources and categorisation details"},{"header":"Total","source":"Eurostat energy balances, EU27 gross electricity generation"},{"header":"Numerator · nrg_bal_peh C0000X0350-0370","source":"Eurostat nrg_bal_peh · geo=EU27_2020, unit=GWH, freq=A, nrg_bal=GEP, siec=C0000X0350-0370 · https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/statistics/1.0/data/nrg_bal_peh?format=JSON&lang=EN&geo=EU27_2020&unit=GWH&freq=A&nrg_bal=GEP&siec=C0000X0350-0370"},{"header":"Numerator · nrg_bal_peh P1000","source":"Eurostat nrg_bal_peh · geo=EU27_2020, unit=GWH, freq=A, nrg_bal=GEP, siec=P1000 · https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/statistics/1.0/data/nrg_bal_peh?format=JSON&lang=EN&geo=EU27_2020&unit=GWH&freq=A&nrg_bal=GEP&siec=P1000"},{"header":"Numerator · nrg_bal_peh S2000","source":"Eurostat nrg_bal_peh · geo=EU27_2020, unit=GWH, freq=A, nrg_bal=GEP, siec=S2000 · https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/statistics/1.0/data/nrg_bal_peh?format=JSON&lang=EN&geo=EU27_2020&unit=GWH&freq=A&nrg_bal=GEP&siec=S2000"},{"header":"Numerator · nrg_bal_peh O4000XBIO","source":"Eurostat nrg_bal_peh · geo=EU27_2020, unit=GWH, freq=A, nrg_bal=GEP, siec=O4000XBIO · https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/statistics/1.0/data/nrg_bal_peh?format=JSON&lang=EN&geo=EU27_2020&unit=GWH&freq=A&nrg_bal=GEP&siec=O4000XBIO"},{"header":"Numerator · nrg_bal_peh G3000","source":"Eurostat nrg_bal_peh · geo=EU27_2020, unit=GWH, freq=A, nrg_bal=GEP, siec=G3000 · https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/statistics/1.0/data/nrg_bal_peh?format=JSON&lang=EN&geo=EU27_2020&unit=GWH&freq=A&nrg_bal=GEP&siec=G3000"},{"header":"Denominator · nrg_bal_peh TOTAL","source":"Eurostat nrg_bal_peh · geo=EU27_2020, unit=GWH, freq=A, nrg_bal=GEP, siec=TOTAL · https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/statistics/1.0/data/nrg_bal_peh?format=JSON&lang=EN&geo=EU27_2020&unit=GWH&freq=A&nrg_bal=GEP&siec=TOTAL"},{"header":"Report baseline 2022 (%)","source":"ESABCC (2024) “Towards EU climate neutrality”, underlying-data workbook — the report''s own 2022 figure, the anchor the later years are spliced onto."},{"header":"Live source at 2022 (same basis as the columns left)","source":"Eurostat nrg_bal_peh · fossil ÷ total gross electricity production · EU27_2020 — the same query, read at 2022; dividing by it cancels the level difference between the source''s scope and the report''s, leaving only the year-on-year change."},{"header":"fraction → % (× 100)","source":"Unit convention: the report workbook computes this share as a fraction, the indicator database stores it as a percent number (migrations 058 / 075 / 076). The conversion is carried here as its own column so the grid and the plotted series agree."}],"rows":[{"year":2005,"cells":[0.5182598412168846,808.8822210000001,548.315303,154.208875,2916.31008,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,100]},{"year":2006,"cells":[0.5190010238230972,816.4990429999999,575.616132,148.089791,2967.6337719999997,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,100]},{"year":2007,"cells":[0.5260279545909439,828.805419,609.4216759999999,130.798327,2982.779542999999,null,null,n